  "complex": {
    "id": "kinetempo-paced-breathing",
    "name": "Paced breathing",
    "description": "Fifteen minutes at six breaths a minute — five seconds in, five seconds out — which is the dose behind the blood-pressure evidence for slow breathing: roughly 4–8 mmHg systolic across trials of ten to fifteen minutes a day. Sit upright and comfortable, breathe through the nose into the belly rather than the chest, and let the timer set the pace instead of counting.\n\nTwo shorter patterns come with this program for other moments: box breathing, 4-4-4-4, to settle before something stressful, and 4-7-8, four cycles, as a wind-down before sleep.\n\nIf the pace feels like a struggle, shorten it — light-headedness or tingling means you are breathing too deeply, not too slowly; stop, breathe normally, and start again with smaller breaths. Slow breathing supports treatment for high blood pressure, it does not replace it, and it is not a treatment for asthma or any breathing condition. Not medical advice.",
    "restBetweenMs": 0,
